{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Around the Fur feels like a natural next choice because its heavy riffs and atmospheric tension connect with what draws me to Tool and heavier alternative rock.",
    "Killers Enhanced, Probot, and Order Of The Black fit my appetite for forceful metal, while Theory of a Deadman matches the melodic hard rock side of my listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Everything You Want and Morph the Cat feel too mellow for this session; being connected to rock does not give them the weight and intensity I want.",
    "Dark Side Of The Moon shares some progressive appeal with Tool, but that connection alone is not enough. The Southern rock of Pronounced and roots-oriented storytelling of Greendale also miss my current mood."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in rock seems to have been stretched to include sounds that feel very different from the heavy albums I have been choosing.",
    "My interest in Tool seems to have been read as a broad appetite for progressive music, when heaviness and tension are important parts of its appeal to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest choices, including Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days, reinforce my current interest in intensity, heavy guitars, and a darker atmosphere.",
    "I enjoy both melodic hard rock and more aggressive metal, but the melody needs enough force behind it to hold my interest right now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in hard rock and metal, but stretched it too broadly into gentler and older rock sounds that do not fit my current mood."
}"}
